  "disagreements": {
    "item": [
      {
        "id": "D-1",
        "severity": "citation",
        "claim": "S524 table's located lines and quotes are correct.",
        "finding": "Four quotes do NOT sit at the cited ranges: mask equal length cited 400-419 -> actual 420; 'value_length % word_size' cited 421-450 -> actual 476; parse_error call cited 749-782 -> actual 784; MIME-Magic memcmp cited 815 -> actual 814. Two more quotes are not verbatim single lines: 'if (i + matchlet->value_length > len) return FALSE;' spans 525-526, and the indent-recursion call spans 571-574."
      },
      {
        "id": "D-2",
        "severity": "MODEL -- can change answers",
        "claim": "Receipt says 'word size 1/2/4'; shared contract says '(1|2|4 only)'; the modulo check rejects value_length % word_size != 0.",
        "finding": "The C (xdgmimemagic.c:440-443) accepts word_size {0,1,2,4} -- 0 IS legal -- and the whole swap+modulo block is guarded by 'if (matchlet->word_size > 1)' at :471, so with 0 or 1 there is NO swap and NO modulo check (for 0 that would be a division by zero). Oracle-measured: '~0' with even length matches; '~0' with ODD length also matches (text/x-ws0odd); '~2' with odd length is rejected (3%2!=0) and drops the section; '~3'/'~5' rejected. A model accepting only {1,2,4} rejects a legal ~0 section the oracle matches; a model applying the modulo check unconditionally divides by zero. The C1 draft in build/ already states the correct rule and matches the oracle on all fixtures -- the defect is in the receipt/contract wording."
      },
      {
        "id": "D-3",
        "severity": "MODEL -- can change answers",
        "claim": "'a reachable mime.cache means cache mode'; 'a case that holds a mime.cache is a cache-mode refusal case'.",
        "finding": "The C's trigger is loadability, not presence: xdgmimecache.c:63-65 (version 1, minor 1..2), :128 (size < 40 -> fail), :137-139 (version check); xdgmime.c:137-154 (a cache that LOADS is added to _caches and that dir's text files are skipped), :180-190 (else magic read as text), :532-535 (if ANY cache loaded -> cache reader only). Oracle-measured: 0-byte, 14-byte, 39-byte and bad-version mime.cache all yield TEXT mode (answered from the magic file); only >=40 bytes with version 1.1/1.2 yields cache mode. So a case fixture holding a short or corrupt mime.cache is answered by the oracle in text mode, but the contract's case rule would label it UNSUPPORTED. The rule must read 'holds a LOADABLE mime.cache'."
      },
      {
        "id": "D-4",
        "severity": "citation",
        "claim": "Fetch dir contains xdgmimemagic.c.1/.2, xdgmime.c.1/.2, smi-ar01s02.html.1/.2, 'two fetches each, both bodies byte-identical'.",
