      },
      {
        "id": "D-5",
        "severity": "citation",
        "claim": "S525's spec-page line numbers all locate their quotes.",
        "finding": "Internally inconsistent: the header quote (387) and the first two rows (389-391, 393-399) ARE raw-HTML line numbers, but the remaining four are not, with the offset growing monotonically through the section 2.5 table -- line form actual 398 vs cited 400-414; two-byte length 403 vs 407-410; defaults 421 vs 429-433; parent rule 426 vs 435-439; unknown char 429 vs 441-446. Consistent with a table-expanded text extraction, but not reproducible with raw-HTML lines, sequential non-empty stripped lines, </td>/</tr>/</p>/</div>/<br> split variants, bs4.get_text, or word-joined windows. All 7 quotes are verbatim present. A row citing 'page line 429-433' points at unrelated text in the fetched file."
      }
    ]
  },
  "additional_finding": {
    "id": "swap-provenance",
    "severity": "citation gap",
    "finding": "The receipt's byte-swap claim is TRUE for this host but under-cited. The swap is under '#if LITTLE_ENDIAN' (xdgmimemagic.c:473, 482) and LITTLE_ENDIAN is NOT a glib build flag -- upstream meson.build defines only g_byte_order/G_LITTLE_ENDIAN for the public glibconfig.h, and gio/xdgmime/meson.build adds only -DHAVE_CONFIG_H and -DXDG_PREFIX. It comes from glibc's <endian.h> (bits/endian.h under __USE_MISC), reached through xdgmimemagic.c's own include set (verified by compiling that include set standalone: LITTLE_ENDIAN IS defined). Arch's glib2 2.90.1-1 PKGBUILD builds with meson, adds no -DLITTLE_ENDIAN, and its two downstream patches touch schemas and terminal names only. The corpus row should cite 471-497 and name the guard, since the swap is host-conditional rather than guaranteed by the C's own build files."
  },
  "oracle_measurements": "Built .ufo/waves/round-95/controls/mimesniff-oracle-r95.c (sha256 99df35f8...4d124a) in scratch; ran env -i LC_ALL=C HOME=<case>/h XDG_DATA_DIRS=<case>/d1. Confirmed: byte swap for word sizes 2/4 (value 01 02 with ~2 matches data 02 01, not 01 02; ~1 does not swap); accepted word sizes {0,1,2,4} with the modulo check only for >1; cache-mode trigger is loadability (>=40 bytes, version 1.1/1.2); error recovery drops the whole section (a bad header also eats the next line, and a junk line can absorb that skip); insert order priority-descending with ties in file order, one global list across dirs in XDG_DATA_DIRS order; tree rules (first matchlet at indent 1 -> never holds; indent 0 -> indent 2 skipped level -> never holds; a holding parent with a failing child fails the section); len 0 -> application/x-zerosize (priority 100); sniffed_prio >= 80 wins outright over a name type (80/90 win, 50/79 do not); 12-byte header gate rejects anything else.",
  "c1_draft_crosscheck": "Copied build/mado-mimetext.c1.py read-only into scratch with its sibling tools/mado-mimeglob.py; compared against the oracle on 116 fixtures this seat constructed covering all the above, in both name=NULL and name=f.txt modes: 116 compared, 0 mismatches. The 4 fixtures the draft refuses are the intended cache-mode refusals and are excluded. The draft is behaviourally correct; the disagreements are in the receipt/contract wording.",
